Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.77,0:00:03.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Back to the compass,\Nand to the two questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.92,0:00:06.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}When will this needle turn?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.02,0:00:09.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}For the Earth, no one can say.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.85,0:00:12.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}In a simple computer\Nmodel, chaos makes the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.60,0:00:15.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}forecast fade before\Nthe average wait ends.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.08,0:00:21.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}But {\c&H00A1ED&}how often{\c&HF7F4F2&} the field flips, counted as\Ncrossings of zero, can still be answered.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.26,0:00:27.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The answer hides in a shoebox of\Nsnapshots, read with the equations.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.71,0:00:33.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}And a {\c&HF09CB4&}machine{\c&HF7F4F2&} can learn to dream such\Nsnapshots, between the simulated settings.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.44,0:00:37.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}On small test problems, it partly works.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.61,0:00:40.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The mirror holds by construction,\Nat every setting.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.02,0:00:43.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}On three dials, the {\c&H00A1ED&}rate of zero crossings{\c&HF7F4F2&}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.68,0:00:47.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}is roughly right far from the\Nthreshold, and poor near it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.99,0:00:51.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}A smooth machine rounds\Noff a steep change.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.44,0:00:54.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The bigger tests,\Nin three dimensions and in the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.45,0:00:57.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}shapes of real machines,\Nare written as bets.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.94,0:01:00.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}One lesson remains.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.70,0:01:03.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Enforce each law where it is true.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.55,0:01:06.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Exactly, where it is exact.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.39,0:01:09.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}{\c&H00A1ED&}On average{\c&HF7F4F2&}, where it\Nonly holds on average.
